<temp_file_path>>6:12:I:28:[shellcheck] SC2086: Double quote to prevent globbing and word splitting.
<temp_file_path>>5:3:W:33:[shell_idiom] `mkdir -p` takes several directories: `mkdir -p $out/a $out/b`
<temp_file_path>>7:7:W:33:[shell_idiom] `$(cat file)`: bash reads it without `cat` as `$(<file)`
<temp_file_path>>2:3:I:33:[shell_idiom] `cat` only feeds `sort`: read the file directly
